# Rhoform-generated and simulation scratch state
.rhoform-cache/
.rhoform-build/
*.raw
*.log
# ...but NOT the evidence files, which are deliberately authored deliverables
# that happen to end in `.log`. `*.log` was written for ngspice scratch output
# and silently swallowed all of them: five `validation.log` files that nine
# tracked documents cite as committed evidence — including `ir/validation.log`,
# which carries a retraction of fabricated evidence — plus the golden harness's
# tamper-evidence ledger, whose own README calls an unledgered golden change an
# error. `git add` on an ignored path does nothing unless forced, so nothing
# ever warned. tests/structure/check-layout.sh now fails if one of these exists
# untracked, so the exclusion cannot come back by accident.
!**/validation.log
!tests/golden/UPDATES.log

# Cross-agent configuration is intentionally versioned. These negations
# override common user-global ignores for Claude and agent configuration.
!.agents/
!.agents/**
!.claude/
!.claude/**
!AGENTS.md
!CLAUDE.md

# ...but the secrets rules above must WIN there too. `!.agents/**` and
# `!.claude/**` are the last matching rule for everything beneath those
# directories, so they re-admitted `.env`, `*.pem`, `*.key` and every cache
# pattern — the negations were written to version skills and instructions and
# they also switched off the secrets section for two whole subtrees. AGENTS.md:
# "Keep credentials ... out of source, skills, Linear, Notion, and Slack."
#
# Re-stated after the negations rather than tightened above them, because the
# negations legitimately need to be broad: the rule that must come last is the
# one that refuses secrets, not the one that admits configuration.
.agents/**/.env
.agents/**/.env.*
.agents/**/*.pem
.agents/**/*.key
.claude/**/.env
.claude/**/.env.*
.claude/**/*.pem
.claude/**/*.key
.agents/**/__pycache__/
.claude/**/__pycache__/
.agents/**/.DS_Store
.claude/**/.DS_Store

# Transient agent worktrees. This must come AFTER the negations above, because
# the last matching rule wins: `!.claude/**` was written to version `.agents/`
# and `.claude/skills/` and also un-ignored this, so a stale worktree sat
# untracked in every `git status` and was one `git add -A` away from being
# committed as a second, pre-rename copy of the whole repository. Which is
# exactly what happened while fixing it.
.claude/worktrees/
